    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-024: Hover-Match Transition Check** — the fix for ADR-023's measured gap: wrapper-element hovers still taking 340-460ms because `restyle()` re-cascades all ~2,191 flagged `<a>` descendants even though **zero** of them transition their `:hover` match state when a wrapper is hovered.\n\n**Documentation only.** Implementation (2 commits + docs) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n## This ADR follows the Meta-lesson: measure first\n\nADR-023's Meta-lesson section (written last cycle) says: *\"ADR Followup predictions must be measurement-first — don't predict a wall-clock number without measuring the input distribution.\"*\n\n**So before writing this ADR, we instrumented and measured.** The instrumentation counted, per hover transition:\n- How many elements the filtered walk flagged (`flagged`)\n- How many of those actually changed their `:hover` match state (`transitioned`)\n- How long the transition check itself takes (`check`)\n\nRun on Wikipedia's HTML article (799KB, 7,871 elements, 158 rules, debug -O0, **72 transitions** during a manual hover session):\n\n| Transition kind | `flagged` | `transitioned` | Check cost |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Wrapper hover (`<html>`, `<body>`) | 2,191 | **0** | 2.5-6.1ms |\n| `<section>` ↔ `<a>` (link hover) | 123 | **1** | 0.3-0.4ms |\n| `<section>` ↔ `<b>`, `<table>` (non-`<a>` in section) | 123 | **0** | 0.2ms |\n| `<span>` inside `<a>` ↔ `<html>` | 2,191 | **1** | 2.6ms |\n| `<button>`, small `<div>` (no `<a>` descendants) | 0-6 | 0 | <0.05ms |\n\n**The ADR-024 premise is confirmed empirically**: wrapper hover flags 2,191 elements, transitions 0. The current implementation cascades all 2,191 — 100% waste.\n\n## Per-element cost analysis (measured, not estimated)\n\n- **Cascade**: 380ms / 2,191 = **~0.17ms per flagged element**\n- **Check**: 4ms / 2,191 = **~0.0018ms per element**\n- **Check is ~95× cheaper than cascade**\n\nEven at 50% transition rate, the check pays for itself. At the measured 0% (wrapper case), it's pure profit.\n\n## The subtle case that shaped the design\n\n`prev=<html> new=<span>` shows `transitioned=1` — a `<span>` is hovered, and its ancestor `<a>` transitions its `a:hover` match from false to true (per ADR-018's walk-up matcher).\n\nA naive optimization like *\"if `hovered_element` isn't an `<a>`, skip cascading entirely\"* would **miss this case**. The check must be **per-element**: \"does *this* element's match state change?\", not \"does the currently-hovered element match an anchor?\"\n\nThis is now a dedicated correctness test in the implementation plan.\n\n## What the ADR specifies\n\n- **New helper**: `matches_any_anchor_hover(el, state, ua, author)` — extracted from `compute_hover_sensitive`'s inner loop, shared by both the precompute and the transition check.\n- **Pipeline integration**: `restyle()` Level 1 path evaluates `old_match` vs `new_match` per flagged element; cascades only if different.\n- **Cache-equality invariant preserved**: if match unchanged, style unchanged, prior cache entry valid. Extended test for the wrapper-hover scenario.\n\n## Expected outcome (measured baseline, not prediction)\n\n| Hover type | ADR-023 measured | ADR-024 target |\n|---|---|---|\n| Link hover | 14-25ms | 14-25ms (unchanged; check adds <1ms) |\n| **Wrapper hover** | **340-460ms** | **~25ms** (walk 5 + check 4 + cascade 0 + propagate 12 + restyle_walk 5) |\n\nThe ~25ms is **arithmetic on measured components**, not a guess — the way ADR-023's \"~20ms\" should have been but wasn't.\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Measurement-first discipline applied** — every number in the Decision section traces to today's instrumentation run, not a prediction.\n- [ ] **The subtle case is real and handled** — `<span>` inside `<a>` transitions the ancestor's match. Per-element check catches it; per-hovered-element would miss it. Dedicated test in the plan.\n- [ ] **~25ms target is grounded** — 5+4+0+12+5 = 26ms, rounded to ~25ms. If the implementation measures differently, the ADR gets updated with the real number (as happened in ADR-022 and ADR-023).\n- [ ] **Scope is small** — extract one helper + one filter in the existing walk + 2-3 tests. ADR-023's primitives (detection, precompute) are already shipped.\n- [ ] **Deferred items are honest** — full subtree walk still runs (5ms), propagate/restyle_walk still full-tree (17ms), Level 2 unchanged. All acknowledged.\n\n## Deferred\n\n- **Level 2 (compound `:hover`) optimization** — still deferred from ADR-023\n- **`prev_hovered_`-aware subtree-walk filtering** — skip walking entirely when the hovered element can't trigger transitions. Deferred; the check already gets wrapper hover to ~25ms (sub-perceptual)\n- **Release build measurements** — debug baseline is the ADR target; release expected 5-10× faster\n- **Cross-hover-transition batching** — not a real bottleneck\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched, so no test changes. Will run `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` after merge to confirm `main` still clean (267 cases, 1140 assertions, unchanged).\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/024-hover-transition-check.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n\nRefs #150\n",
